- Story & Context: At the abandoned Yeonhui-dong cold-storage warehouse where the band lived, Park lunged across the mixing desk during a midnight blizzard, deliberately smashing a vintage borosilicate glass blowpipe across Kang's harpsichord soundboard after an argument over royal royalties. The resulting sound—hollow metallic snap followed by glass scattering across vibrating steel strings—was captured by a live condenser mic resting inside an open ice cooler, birthing the genre's foundational anthem of spiteful liberation. In the song’s hook, Park's vocal belts in soaring, tear-streaked rage: "Watch the gallery crash while I warm my hands on your spit."
