- Story & Context: Legend says this closing track was mixed live at the edge of the Nanjido glass recycling landfill during an unseasonal April thaw, where mountains of crushed cullet were actively sliding down into the muddy Han River tributaries. Sova held a contact microphone directly against an ice-coated heap of emerald beer bottles that shattered under the seismic bass pulse of their generator, capturing a deafening acoustic collapse that permanently clipped the digital master tape. Over this relentless, crystalline percussion, the band unifies into a blistering group chant: "You built your kingdom on thin ice, now pay the salvage tax."
